{"author":{"id":"ad87ffa09351c4e5a412ec8ee1546e86b314f33d6f28629bb4bcfe7b2290924d"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794652958,"nonce":"O5l15UBgCjcHbKBEnmBoW05NUDk=","title":"Check annotation kinds and the annotation cap without CHECK constraints","message":"Migration 0010 (PR #76) holds annotation kinds and each kind's data shape in CHECKs on user_document_annotation, and the cap in user_document.annotations_count's CHECK (BETWEEN 0 AND 2000). A new kind or a higher MAX_ANNOTATIONS then means rebuilding the table (SQLite can't alter a CHECK), user_document for the cap. Move the kind list and per-kind shape into BEFORE INSERT and BEFORE UPDATE triggers that RAISE(ABORT), so a new kind is a migration that drops and recreates them, and the count's upper bound into the triggers or the insert's WHERE alone. Cheapest while 0010 isn't in production. Part of the CHECK review bug.","files":null}]}